# `{ ...state, extra: v }` makes another layout than its source has. Behind the tests of the source's shape, order of keys and want of other properties the fields were read one by one and a
# NewObject took them all: a record of K fields cost K reads and K stores of code at each place. Where each field lies in line in both cells in one representation the copy is one operation: the emitter
# lays the two plans of slots side by side and copies each run of words that follow one another in both cells, in a loop where the run is long, into a cell that is born with those fields.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = HasKeyOrder
# CHECK: = HasNoExtraProperties
# CHECK: = NewObject layout=
# CHECK-NEXT: = TryCopyFields {{*}} sourceLayout=
# CHECK-NOT: = GetSlot
# -- source: main.ts
